  "workflow_name": "Steady-state thermoelectric module performance evaluation",
  "definition": "This workflow models a thermoelectric module (TEG or TEC) under steady-state conditions, incorporating thermal contact resistances and temperature-dependent material properties. It sets up heat balance equations at the hot and cold junctions, relates internal junction temperatures to externally measurable temperatures via thermal resistance networks, and solves the coupled nonlinear system iteratively to compute performance metrics such as electrical power, heat flows, coefficient of performance, and efficiency. The workflow supports parameter sweeps over geometric (leg height, fill factor, number of leg pairs) and operating (current, heat flux, heat transfer coefficient) variables to analyze and optimize module performance.",
